# this container's mounts + service, both lanes  (vLLM)
#
# build-spec — per-port runtime declaration, sourced by the shared resolver.
# Baked at /opt/resources/build-spec. See base/resolve/build-spec.example for the
# full contract. SOURCED bash: plain arrays/vars, zero dependencies.

# ── SERVICE (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vLLM serves the model named in the config file. $DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG is a deliberate
# env knob (a config-file SELECTOR with a smart default — not a raw path the user must
# know); $VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS (folded in by PRE_LAUNCH below) is the other. Default =
# the persisted /opt/data copy that templates.yaml seeds (if_missing) from the shipped
# template. User may point it elsewhere.
#
# ⚠️ IT IS OURS, NOT UPSTREAM'S — it is not in vllm/envs.py, and argparse_utils.py
# reads only the `--config` FLAG. So it carries the DROSTE_ prefix like every other
# droste-owned setting, and the OLD `VLLM_CONFIG` spelling is simply gone (no backward
# compatibility is owed; a native VLLM_* spelling would be, this was never one).
# ⚠️ Substring noise — VLLM_CONFIG_ROOT and VLLM_CONFIGURE_LOGGING are real and
# UNRELATED upstream variables. A bare grep for VLLM_CONFIG is untrustworthy.
#
# 🚨 A CONFIG WITH NO MODEL DOES NOT FAIL. This comment used to say vLLM exits with
# "model is required"; it does not. ModelConfig.model defaults to Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B
# (config/model.py:103), `model_tag` is nargs="?", and validate_parsed_serve_args
# never checks — so an unedited box DOWNLOADS AND SERVES Qwen3-0.6B and reads
# HEALTHY. What to do about that is a ruling, not a wiring decision (board N21);
# recorded here so the next reader does not inherit the false version.
: "${DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG:=/opt/data/vllm_config.yaml}"
export DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG
SERVICE=( vllm serve --config "$DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG" )

# ── HEALTH — probe endpoint for droste-healthcheck.sh ────────────────────────
# vLLM's OpenAI server exposes /health (200 when the engine is ready). Weight
# load + graph work happens before it answers, so the podman
# --health-start-period must cover it.
HEALTH_PATH="/health"
HEALTH_ACCEPT="ok"

# ── ENV_FILE (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Seeded from templates/vllm.env (templates.yaml if_missing). vLLM's SERVE FLAGS
# live in the YAML consumed via --config; this file carries the ~209 runtime
# VLLM_* ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES, which are not expressible as YAML keys — several
# are read before any config is parsed. Two mechanisms, so two files.
#
# ⚠️ It is also the only place $VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS and $DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG can be set.
# Both were advertised by this box (here and in the generated YAML header) while no
# file existed to hold them, which made the catch-all itself unreachable in the
# lane that serves. server.env cannot stand in: it is read in a subshell whose
# output is discarded except for three keys.
#
# ⭐ ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING AND ALREADY CORRECT: the resolver sources this file
# AFTER the build-spec and BEFORE PRE_LAUNCH, and PRE_LAUNCH re-reads
# $DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG when it rebuilds SERVICE — so a user's DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG here
# wins over the default set at the top of this file. Do not move the
# `: "${DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG:=...}"` line into PRE_LAUNCH, and do not hardcode the path
# in the rebuild.
# ▶ OPEN QUESTION, NOT RESOLVED HERE: vllm.env's Reserved section lists
#   DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG among the settings a user must NOT set, while this block says
#   a user's value wins. Both cannot be true. TODAY'S BEHAVIOUR IS "the user's value
#   wins" and this wiring keeps it unchanged; the disagreement is queued for a
#   ruling, not settled by whoever edits next.
#
# ⭐ AND IT IS SOURCED UNDER `set -a`, WHICH IS WHY NATIVE LINES NEED NO WIRING.
# Every `VLLM_FOO=bar` a user uncomments is exported by the resolver itself. Only
# the DROSTE_VLLM_* names below need translating — they are the settings where
# passing the user's word through unprocessed would be wrong or fatal.
ENV_FILE="/opt/data/vllm.env"

# ── OVERLAYS (optional) — <upper>:<lower> ────────────────────────────────────
# Overlay the persisted upper over the WHOLE baked venv (captures bin/ console
# scripts too and avoids pinning a pythonX.Y path) so user pip installs persist
# without shadowing the baked torch/vllm stack. The upper is CACHE class (a pip
# install is re-runnable) → /opt/program-cache, which the installer may empty.
OVERLAYS=(
    "/opt/program-cache/venv:/opt/venv"
)

# ── SURFACES (optional) — <src>:<dest> ───────────────────────────────────────
# No container-specific state surfaces beyond caches/config for vLLM.
SURFACES=()

# ── CACHES (optional) — <src>:<dest> ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Persist the torch-stack compute/kernel caches under /opt/program-cache/compute/ with
# zero env vars ($HOME-relative dests so both lanes resolve correctly). THE compute/
# PREFIX IS LOAD-BEARING: it is what the resolver rewrites to the shared /opt/caches
# store when that volume is bound. Triton default cache is ~/.triton/cache (01-rocm-env-
# for-triton.sh sets no TRITON_CACHE_DIR, so the default holds). MIOpen's miopen-db
# row is its machine-written tuning DB (~/.config/miopen is MIOpen's default userdb
# path) in addition to the ~/.cache/miopen kernel cache. The vllm row is vLLM's own
# compile/artifact cache (~/.cache/vllm) — it consciously joins the shared
# /opt/caches store under the v0.2.0 cache policy (owner decision 2026-07-09).
CACHES=(
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/miopen:$HOME/.cache/miopen"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/miopen-db:$HOME/.config/miopen"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/triton:$HOME/.triton/cache"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/vllm:$HOME/.cache/vllm"
)

# ── CRITICAL (optional) — <label>:<path> ─────────────────────────────────────
# HF cache is CRITICAL: unbound => vLLM silently re-downloads multi-GB weights into an
# anonymous volume that vanishes on recreate. Hard-error unless ALLOW_EPHEMERAL.
CRITICAL=(
    "hf-cache:$HOME/.cache/huggingface"
)

# ── OPTIONAL (optional) — <label>:<path>[:<marker>] ──────────────────────────
# A directory of local weights the user may bind; tell-once, don't nag. vLLM can serve a
# model by absolute path (model: /opt/models/...) in the config. Marker body:
# templates/mount_shared_models_here.
OPTIONAL=(
    "models:/opt/models:/opt/models/mount_shared_models_here"
)

# ── The vllm.env → environment table ─────────────────────────────────────────
# vllm.env offers yes/no (or a short menu); vLLM reads its own variables from the
# environment. This table is the translation, and it is the ONLY mapping — adding a
# setting means editing vllm.env AND this file.
#
# 🚨 THERE IS NO SINGLE WIRE VALUE THAT WORKS FOR ALL OF THEM, which is the whole
# reason these are droste-owned rather than passed through. vLLM's own env table
# uses SIX incompatible boolean readers, measured at the pin (vllm/envs.py, v0.16.0):
#
#   bool(int(x))                  "1" only — "true" raises ValueError, server dies
#   .lower() in ("true","1")       either
#   .lower() == "true"             "true" ONLY — "1" reads as False
#   == "1"                         "1" ONLY — "true" reads as False
#   .strip().lower() in ('1','true')  either, and it strips surrounding space
#   is_true() (huggingface_hub's)  upper-cases, matches {1,ON,YES,TRUE}
#
# So the true/false spelling is PER VARIABLE. A user writing `yes` would hit a
# ValueError on the bool(int) rows and a silent False on several others; that is
# exactly the fall-through we do not make users carry.
#
# "<SUFFIX>:<native var>:<ON wire>:<OFF wire>" — ours is DROSTE_VLLM_<SUFFIX>.
#
# ⚠️ THE COLUMNS ARE "WHAT WE WRITE WHEN THE USER SAYS ON/OFF", NOT "TRUE/FALSE".
# Five rows are marked INVERTED: upstream spells the setting as a DISABLE/SKIP, so
# the user's `on` writes a 0. That is not a typo and swapping it back silently
# inverts a working box. Each one names the upstream variable it flips.
VLLM_BOOL_VARS=(
    # ── Model sources ──
    # huggingface_hub's is_true(), not vLLM's: {"1","ON","YES","TRUE"} upper-cased
    "HF_HUB_OFFLINE:HF_HUB_OFFLINE:1:0"
    # .lower() == "true" — "1" would read as FALSE here
    "USE_MODELSCOPE:VLLM_USE_MODELSCOPE:true:false"
    # ── LoRA adapters ── .strip().lower() in ('1','true')
    "RT_LORA_UPDATES_OK:VLLM_ALLOW_RUNTIME_LORA_UPDATING:1:0"
    # ── Caches & config ── bool(int) ×3, == "1" ×1
    "USE_TRITON_AWQ:VLLM_USE_TRITON_AWQ:1:0"
    "DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE:VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE:1:0"
    "ASSETS_CACHE_MODEL_CLEAN:VLLM_ASSETS_CACHE_MODEL_CLEAN:1:0"
    "V1_USE_OUTLINES_CACHE:VLLM_V1_USE_OUTLINES_CACHE:1:0"
    # ── Server liveness ── bool(int)
    "KEEP_ALIVE:VLLM_KEEP_ALIVE_ON_ENGINE_DEATH:1:0"
    # ── Tuning ──
    # .strip().lower() in ('1','true'). ⚠️ NOT a quality knob: exceeding the derived
    # length gives nan (RoPE) or a device-side out-of-bounds error. It only downgrades
    # a startup ValueError to a warning.
    "LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN_OK:VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN:1:0"
    # ours, read by this image's patched FP8 kernels — not in vllm/envs.py
    "STRIX_FP8_TRITON:VLLM_STRIX_FP8_TRITON:1:0"
    # ── ROCm per-kernel toggles ── bool(int) ×2, .lower() in ("true","1") ×1
    "ROCM_FP8_PADDING:VLLM_ROCM_FP8_PADDING:1:0"
    "ROCM_MOE_PADDING:VLLM_ROCM_MOE_PADDING:1:0"
    "ROCM_CUSTOM_PAGED_ATTN:VLLM_ROCM_CUSTOM_PAGED_ATTN:1:0"
    # ── Idle behaviour ── bool(int)
    "SLEEP_WHEN_IDLE:VLLM_SLEEP_WHEN_IDLE:1:0"
    # ── Security ── bool(int)   (DO_NOT_TRACK is special-cased below: two variables)
    "INSEC_SERIAL_OK:VLLM_ALLOW_INSECURE_SERIALIZATION:1:0"
    # ── API, tool calling & parsing ── bool(int) ×3
    "RESPONSES_API_STORE:VLLM_ENABLE_RESPONSES_API_STORE:1:0"
    "TOOL_JSON_ERROR_AUTOMATIC_RETRY:VLLM_TOOL_JSON_ERROR_AUTOMATIC_RETRY:1:0"
    "GPT_OSS_HARMONY_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTIONS_OK:VLLM_GPT_OSS_HARMONY_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTIONS:1:0"
    # ── MoE models ── bool(int) ×4
    "FUSED_MOE_GROUPED_TOPK:VLLM_USE_FUSED_MOE_GROUPED_TOPK:1:0"
    "FUSED_MOE_ACTIVATION_CHUNKING:VLLM_ENABLE_FUSED_MOE_ACTIVATION_CHUNKING:1:0"
    "MOE_DP_CHUNK:VLLM_ENABLE_MOE_DP_CHUNK:1:0"
    "SHARED_EXPERTS_STREAM:VLLM_DISABLE_SHARED_EXPERTS_STREAM:0:1"   # INVERTED (DISABLE_)
    # ── KV cache & attention ──
    "USE_MLA:VLLM_MLA_DISABLE:0:1"                                   # INVERTED (_DISABLE)
    "ROCM_FP8_MFMA_PAGE_ATTN:VLLM_ROCM_FP8_MFMA_PAGE_ATTN:1:0"
    "CHUNKED_LOCAL_ATTN_WITH_HYBRID_KV_CACHE_OK:VLLM_ALLOW_CHUNKED_LOCAL_ATTN_WITH_HYBRID_KV_CACHE:1:0"
    # ── Multimodal input ── bool(int)
    "MEDIA_REDIRECTS_OK:VLLM_MEDIA_URL_ALLOW_REDIRECTS:1:0"
    # ── Multi-node serving ──
    # .lower() in ("true","1") — "1" chosen for consistency with its neighbours
    "PYNCCL:VLLM_DISABLE_PYNCCL:0:1"                                 # INVERTED (DISABLE_)
    "P2P_CHECK:VLLM_SKIP_P2P_CHECK:0:1"                              # INVERTED (SKIP_)
    "RANDOMIZE_DP_DUMMY_INPUTS:VLLM_RANDOMIZE_DP_DUMMY_INPUTS:1:0"
    "RAY_COMPILED_DAG_OVERLAP_COMM:VLLM_USE_RAY_COMPILED_DAG_OVERLAP_COMM:1:0"
    "RAY_WRAPPED_PP_COMM:VLLM_USE_RAY_WRAPPED_PP_COMM:1:0"
    # ── Compilation & startup cost ── (AOT_COMPILE is tri-state, special-cased below)
    "FORCE_AOT_LOAD:VLLM_FORCE_AOT_LOAD:1:0"
    "MEGA_AOT_ARTIFACT:VLLM_USE_MEGA_AOT_ARTIFACT:1:0"
    "INDUCTOR_MAX_AUTOTUNE:VLLM_ENABLE_INDUCTOR_MAX_AUTOTUNE:1:0"
    "INDUCTOR_COORDINATE_DESCENT_TUNING:VLLM_ENABLE_INDUCTOR_COORDINATE_DESCENT_TUNING:1:0"
    "STANDALONE_COMPILE:VLLM_USE_STANDALONE_COMPILE:1:0"
    "BYTECODE_HOOK:VLLM_USE_BYTECODE_HOOK:1:0"
    # ── Logging ── (LEVEL/COLOR/STREAM are menus, special-cased below)
    "CONFIGURE_LOGGING:VLLM_CONFIGURE_LOGGING:1:0"
    "DEBUG_LOG_API_SRV_RESP:VLLM_DEBUG_LOG_API_SERVER_RESPONSE:true:false"
    "LOG_LOGO:VLLM_DISABLE_LOG_LOGO:0:1"                             # INVERTED (DISABLE_)
    # ── Tracing & diagnostics ──
    # int(), not bool(int): a level, but the file offers the on/off it is used as
    "TRACE_FUNCTION:VLLM_TRACE_FUNCTION:1:0"
    # a STRING upstream (""/"0" off · "1" on · JSON for detail); malformed = silent off
    "GC_DEBUG:VLLM_GC_DEBUG:1:0"
    "DEBUG_WORKSPACE:VLLM_DEBUG_WORKSPACE:1:0"
    "LOG_MODEL_INSPECTION:VLLM_LOG_MODEL_INSPECTION:1:0"
    "DEBUG_MFU_METRICS:VLLM_DEBUG_MFU_METRICS:1:0"
    "COMPUTE_NANS_IN_LOGITS:VLLM_COMPUTE_NANS_IN_LOGITS:1:0"
    "CUSTOM_SCOPES_FOR_PROFILING:VLLM_CUSTOM_SCOPES_FOR_PROFILING:1:0"
    # ── Development ── bool(int) ×2
    "SERVER_DEV_MODE:VLLM_SERVER_DEV_MODE:1:0"
    "USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER:VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER:1:0"
    # ── Experimental ── bool(int) ×1, .lower() in ("true","1") ×2
    "EXPERIMENTAL_PARSER_CONTEXT:VLLM_USE_EXPERIMENTAL_PARSER_CONTEXT:1:0"
    "ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTENTION:VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTENTION:1:0"
    "ROCM_AITER:VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER:1:0"
)

# ── vllm_menu / vllm_pick — the settings whose answer is a MENU, not a bool ──
#
# ⭐ WHY A SEPARATE MECHANISM. A boolean has two answers and both are always
# expressible. A menu has N, and for several of these ONE MEMBER MEANS "DO NOT SET
# THE VARIABLE AT ALL" — VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT is validated by env_with_choices()
# against ["NHD","HND"], which RAISES ValueError for any other value INCLUDING the
# empty string, so `auto` cannot be spelled on the wire: it has to be an absence.
# A wire of "-" is exactly that instruction.
#
# vllm_pick <SUFFIX> <user value> <member=wire> … — prints the wire, or warns and
# fails. The user's value is case-folded and space-stripped (`Auto`, `AUTO ` are
# what people type); the WIRE is emitted verbatim, because upstream's own
# validation is case-SENSITIVE.
vllm_pick() {
    # `given` keeps the user's ORIGINAL spelling for the message — `$2` is a menu
    # member by the time the loop runs, and quoting one of those back at a user who
    # never typed it is worse than saying nothing.
    local suffix=$1 given=$2 val=$2; shift 2
    local pair menu=""
    val=${val,,}; val=${val// /}
    for pair in "$@"; do
        menu="$menu ${pair%%=*}"
        [ "${pair%%=*}" = "$val" ] && { printf '%s' "${pair#*=}"; return 0; }
    done
    serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_$suffix='$given' is not one of:$menu — leaving the setting at its default. Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box."
    return 1
}

# vllm_menu <SUFFIX> <native var> <member=wire> … — the whole read/validate/export.
vllm_menu() {
    local suffix=$1 var=$2; shift 2
    local ref="DROSTE_VLLM_$suffix" val wire
    val=${!ref:-}
    # Unset/blank leaves the native variable alone, exactly as for the booleans.
    [ -n "$val" ] || return 0
    wire=$(vllm_pick "$suffix" "$val" "$@") || return 0
    [ "$wire" = "-" ] && return 0
    export "$var=$wire"
}

# vllm_env — DROSTE_VLLM_* → the native variables, exported for the served process.
# Its own function so it can be driven alone (source the spec, call it, print the
# environment) without building the argv.
# ⚠️ EXPORT IS REQUIRED. resolve::apply_spec runs `set +a` before PRE_LAUNCH, so a
# bare assignment here would never reach the vLLM process — it would be a silent
# no-op, which is the same defect in a different costume.
vllm_env() {
    local entry suffix rest var on off val

    # ── the booleans ──
    for entry in "${VLLM_BOOL_VARS[@]}"; do
        suffix=${entry%%:*}; rest=${entry#*:}
        var=${rest%%:*};     rest=${rest#*:}
        on=${rest%%:*};      off=${rest#*:}
        val="DROSTE_VLLM_$suffix"; val=${!val:-}
        # Unset/blank leaves the variable alone: the image's baked value or vLLM's
        # own default stands. Setting it here would turn an opt-out into an opt-in.
        [ -n "$val" ] || continue
        # droste::bool normalises BOTH user vocabularies to one internal answer, so
        # there are two arms here and not four. yes/no and on/off are not synonyms
        # in the FILE — one answers a question ("never reach the network?"), the
        # other names a state ("padding is on") — and each setting is worded as
        # whichever it actually is. That distinction is the user's to read; by the
        # time a value reaches here it has been resolved and the wording is spent.
        case "$(droste::bool "$val")" in
            on)  export "$var=$on" ;;
            off) export "$var=$off" ;;
            *) serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_$suffix='$val' is not a yes/no or on/off value — leaving $var as it is. Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box." ;;
        esac
    done

    # ── the menus ──
    #
    # 🚨 KV_CACHE_LAYOUT AND VIDEO_LOAD_BACKEND ARE THE SAME DEFECT WITH OPPOSITE
    # FIXES — DO NOT UNIFY THEM. The layout is a CLOSED ENUM: the valid names are a
    # literal list in vllm/envs.py, nothing can add to it, so an unknown value is a
    # typo and the right answer is to whitelist. The video backend is an OPEN
    # REGISTRY: a plugin may register a loader under any name, so at PRE_LAUNCH time
    # a typo and a legitimate plugin name are INDISTINGUISHABLE and refusing would
    # break a working deployment. Whitelist the closed one; pass the open one
    # through with a warning. (See the VIDEO_LOAD_BACKEND block below.)
    #
    # `auto` = "do not set it": env_with_choices raises for anything outside
    # NHD/HND, and that includes both `auto` and the empty string.
    vllm_menu KV_CACHE_LAYOUT VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT auto=- nhd=NHD hnd=HND

    # `auto` here is upstream's own COMPUTED default (torch version + whether the
    # compile cache is disabled), so it likewise has to be an absence — there is no
    # literal that means "work it out yourself".
    vllm_menu AOT_COMPILE VLLM_USE_AOT_COMPILE auto=- on=1 off=0

    # ⚠️ `notset` IS NOT "unset". Python resolves NOTSET on a handler by walking up
    # to the root logger's effective level, which lands on WARNING — QUIETER than
    # leaving the variable alone (unset ⇒ vLLM's own "INFO"). Two "unsets" one layer
    # apart, and the file offers the one that surprises people. Upstream .upper()s
    # the value, so the wire is the canonical spelling.
    vllm_menu LOGGING_LEVEL VLLM_LOGGING_LEVEL \
        debug=DEBUG info=INFO warning=WARNING warn=WARN \
        error=ERROR critical=CRITICAL fatal=FATAL notset=NOTSET

    # ⚠️ THE NATIVE VARIABLE IS NOT A WORD, IT IS A DIGIT. logger.py:30-38 tests
    # `== "0"` then `== "1"` and treats EVERYTHING ELSE as auto — so `always` and
    # `never`, the words a person would reach for, both silently mean auto. That is
    # the whole reason this one is droste-named. `auto` is wired to the literal
    # upstream default rather than to "-" because writing it is faithful: it names
    # the isatty branch that upstream itself falls through to.
    # (NO_COLOR is honoured by upstream ahead of all three; we do not touch it.)
    vllm_menu LOGGING_COLOR VLLM_LOGGING_COLOR auto=auto always=1 never=0

    # ⚠️ The native value is a logging-dictConfig `ext://` REFERENCE, not a word.
    # A value that resolves to a non-stream object configures CLEANLY and then
    # AttributeErrors on every single log record; only an unresolvable ext:// fails
    # at startup. So the menu is closed and short on purpose.
    vllm_menu LOGGING_STREAM VLLM_LOGGING_STREAM \
        stdout=ext://sys.stdout stderr=ext://sys.stderr

    # ── the settings that are not a bool and not a menu ──

    # 🚨 ONE ANSWER, TWO VARIABLES — AND THE "OFF" WIRE IS AN ABSENCE.
    # vLLM reads `VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK or DO_NOT_TRACK or "0"` and compares to "1"
    # (envs.py:629-634). Python's `or` SELECTS the first non-EMPTY operand, so
    # writing VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK=0 would MASK a bare DO_NOT_TRACK=1 the user set for
    # every tool on the machine — a privacy setting silently reversed by us. So
    # `no` UNSETS ours and lets the generic one through, and only VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS
    # (which has no such chain, and which the IMAGE bakes to 1) is written to 0.
    # ⚠️ There is a third opt-out we do not manage: a file at
    # $VLLM_CONFIG_ROOT/do_not_track. This image does not persist ~/.config/vllm.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK:-}
    if [ -n "$val" ]; then
        case "$(droste::bool "$val")" in
            on)  export VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK=1 VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1 ;;
            off) unset VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK; export VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=0 ;;
            *) serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK='$val' is not a yes/no value — leaving telemetry as the image set it (opted out). Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box." ;;
        esac
    fi

    # OPEN REGISTRY (see the note above): warn, then pass through VERBATIM — no
    # case folding, because a registry key is matched exactly. The three names below
    # are what vLLM itself ships at the pin; a plugin may add more, and a name that
    # nothing registers fails with an AssertionError during startup.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_VIDEO_LOAD_BACKEND:-}
    if [ -n "$val" ]; then
        case "$val" in
            opencv|opencv_dynamic|molmo2) ;;
            *) serve::warn "DROSTE_VLLM_VIDEO_LOAD_BACKEND='$val' is not one of the loaders vLLM ships (opencv, opencv_dynamic, molmo2). Passing it through in case a plugin registers it — if nothing does, startup fails with an AssertionError." ;;
        esac
        export VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BACKEND="$val"
    fi

    # A PATH, not a switch — vllm.env:320 shows it BLANK and offers no menu, so the
    # value goes through verbatim and blank is the off-state.
    # 🚨 AND THE OFF-STATE HAS TO BE AN ABSENCE, NOT AN EMPTY STRING. envs.py:573
    # reads `os.environ.get("VLLM_DEBUG_DUMP_PATH", None)` and the default is
    # `str | None = None` (envs.py:218), so a blank is NOT None and every
    # `is not None` gate downstream fires on it. Exporting the blank the file shows
    # would switch the mechanism on and dump to "" — which is why the guard below is
    # load-bearing rather than tidiness.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_DEBUG_DUMP_PATH:-}
    [ -n "$val" ] && export VLLM_DEBUG_DUMP_PATH="$val"

    # ⚠️ int(), so a non-numeric value is a ValueError at import — before any log
    # line the user could read. Digits only, and we refuse rather than guess.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_TOOL_PARSE_REGEX_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-}
    if [ -n "$val" ]; then
        case "$val" in
            ''|*[!0-9]*) serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_TOOL_PARSE_REGEX_TIMEOUT_SECONDS='$val' is not a whole number of seconds — leaving it at vLLM's default of 1. Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box." ;;
            *) export VLLM_TOOL_PARSE_REGEX_TIMEOUT_SECONDS="$val" ;;
        esac
    fi

    # 🚨 THE VALUE IS THE NAME OF AN fx GRAPH NODE, AND THE GATE IS `is not None`.
    # pass_manager.py:61-63 forwards whatever it finds to torch's
    # TORCHINDUCTOR_PATTERN_MATCH_DEBUG, and torch compares it `== node.name`
    # (_inductor/pattern_matcher.py:1979). envs.py:573-574 reads
    # `os.environ.get("VLLM_PATTERN_MATCH_DEBUG", None)` against a `str | None = None`
    # default (envs.py:217), so an EMPTY value is NOT None: it switches the mechanism
    # on and then matches no node. **The blank vllm.env:321 shows must reach the wire
    # as an ABSENCE**, which is exactly what the `-n` guard does.
    # ⭐ A PLAIN VALUE SETTING, NOT A BOOLEAN (vllm.env, s56 — Jei moved this line and
    # DEBUG_DUMP_PATH OUT of the `{on, off*}` block above them). It therefore has no
    # menu, takes no on/off, and MUST NOT warn about one: `on` is simply a node name
    # that nothing will match, and second-guessing the user's node name is not ours to
    # do. The earlier bool-parsing version refused `on` and read `off` as "unset" —
    # both are gone with the menu that justified them.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_PATTERN_MATCH_DEBUG:-}
    [ -n "$val" ] && export VLLM_PATTERN_MATCH_DEBUG="$val"
    # ⚠️ `[ -n … ] && …` returns non-zero on a blank, and this is the LAST command in
    # the function — under `set -e` in both lanes that would fail PRE_LAUNCH for every
    # box that never set the variable, i.e. all of them. Return success explicitly.
    return 0
}

# ── PRE_LAUNCH (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVICE-rebuild (see build-spec.example): fold $VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS into the argv —
# CLI args placed after --config override the config file's values (vLLM's own
# CLI-over-config merge), exactly as the generated config header documents.
# The model rides the config; stale-graph handling is a documented one-liner
# (compile cache is disabled), not an automated pre-launch step.
PRE_LAUNCH="vllm_pre_launch"
vllm_pre_launch() {
    vllm_env

    # Quote-aware split (droste::split_args): a value may contain spaces.
    # shellcheck disable=SC2206
    mapfile -d '' -t _extra < <(droste::split_args "${VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS:-}")
    SERVICE=( vllm serve --config "$DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG" ${_extra[@]+"${_extra[@]}"} )
}
